            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load(\"vectors.npy\").astype(np.float64)\n\n    # Compute squared Euclidean norms of each row\n    norms_sq = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix: G = X @ X.T\n    G = X @ X.T\n\n    # Compute squared distance matrix in-place: ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2<u, v>\n    G *= -2.0\n    G += norms_sq[:, None]\n    G += norms_sq[None, :]\n\n    # Eliminate small negative values caused by numerical inaccuracy and zero the diagonal\n    np.maximum(G, 0.0, out=G)\n    np.fill_diagonal(G, 0.0)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distances\n    np.sqrt(G, out=G)\n\n    total = np.sum(G)\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
